 17592186428937 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428938 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428939 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428940 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428941 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428942 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1033 317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7280f087-059d-5524-8f8b-a1fe79b4ef9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064099 #edb/ref 1069 "e-491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064099 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064099 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064099 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064100 #edb/ref 1069 "e-492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064100 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064100 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064117 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6209" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064117 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064117 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064117 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064245 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175