n" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064246 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064246 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064274 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186065160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186065114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064413 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8829b364-1582-5e1a-894c-d8837d69b705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064509 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064509 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14437" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064509 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064509 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064509 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "36f423a0-7a02-5e68-b537-f427610136e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064509 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064877 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186332487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064877 #edb/ref 1069 "q-49664" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064877 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064877 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064877 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d08b82b1-573b-56aa-9196-6973e5625acf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064877 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)]+[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0]+[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065114 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065114 #edb/ref 1061 1725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065114 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66772855-684d-5b86-b797-dd142c5cce75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065114 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065115 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065115 #edb/ref 1061 1726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065115 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "69d17961-eefe-570a-b3a8-ada39be9dbe8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065115 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065116 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065116 #edb/ref 1061 1730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065116 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7e9ca4a9-f3b8-546c-b51a-bb8c5db61861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065116 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065117 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065117 #edb/ref 1061 1733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065117 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "45eefd0d-11c7-5c51-857d-c39e7a530c49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065117 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065118 #edb/ref 1061 1734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065118 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "26fab519-16d1-54c6-997b-34fc2c75ed86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065118 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065160 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065160 #edb/ref 1061 23242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065160 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e0fec13f-785e-56e3-8799-8139e2f41c60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065160 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065444 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we introduce a method of integration that can be used in cases where integration by substitution fails. The method is known as **integration by parts**. The so-called **by-parts formula** is \n\n$$\n\\int u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis method is handy for integrating products of functions where one factor can be easily integrated, and the other factor can easily be differentiated. \n\nLet's see how to apply it to evaluate the integral \n\n$$\n\\int xe^{2x} \\textrm{d}x\\,.\n$$\n\nThe idea is to call one of the factors $u,$ the other factor $v',$ and then apply the by-parts formula. We'll choose the following:\n\n$$\n\\int \\underbrace{\\color{blue}x}_{\\large\\color{blue}u}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\color{red}e^{2x}}_{\\large\\color{red}v'} \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, if ${\\color{blue}u} = {\\color{blue}x}$ then we differentiate to get ${\\color{blue}u'} = {\\color{blue}1}.$ And if ${\\color{red}v'} = {\\color{red}e^{2x}}$ then we integrate to get ${\\color{red}v} = {\\color{red}\\dfrac{1}{2}e^{2x}}.$ Note that we don't bother with the constant of integration here.\n\nWe now have everything we need, so we can substitute into the \"by-parts\" formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {{x\\cdot {e}^{2x}}_{⏟}}_{u{v}^{'}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={{x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}}_{⏟}}_{uv}-\\int {{\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}\\cdot 1}_{⏟}}_{v{u}^{'}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{2x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{2x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{2x}-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2x}(2x-1)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we're done! Notice that integration by parts allows us to take a complicated integral $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{2x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$ and replace it with the simpler $\\displaystyle \\int e^{2x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$ plus some additional terms." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065444 #edb/ref 1065 892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065444 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7ef18e8c-9fd4-5e14-84ee-a8fe309425c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065444 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065445 #edb/ref 1064 "If you thought the by-parts formula looked similar to the product rule for differentiation, then you'd be right. In fact, that's precisely where it comes from!\n\nTo work out the formula, we recall the product rule for differentiation,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(uv)=u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}+ v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x},\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ and $v$ are functions of $x.$ \n\nIf we rearrange this formula a bit, we get\n\n$$\nu\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(uv)- v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's now integrate both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\int u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}\\,\\textrm{d}x=\\int\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(uv)\\,\\textrm{d}x- \\int v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nUsing the fundamental theorem of calculus, we can use the fact that $\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(uv)\\,\\textrm{d}x=uv,$ and we arrive at the by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065445 #edb/ref 1065 895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065445 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9f435fc9-cb87-577b-89e1-cda2ce506387" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065445 #edb/ref 1067 "Deriving the By Parts Formula From the Product Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065446 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's go back to our first example,\n\n$$\n\\int xe^{2x} \\textrm{d}x\\,.\n$$\n\nNote that when we selected our $u$ and $v',$ we could have picked them the other way around. So instead, we could have said\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{'}=2{e}^{2x} \\\\ {v}^{'}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the by-parts formula using this selection, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{2x}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}-\\int {x}^{2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, while the above is a mathematically correct statement, the integral on the right-hand side is *more* complicated than the integral we started with. Ouch!\n\nTherefore, it's crucial that we select our $u$ and $v'$ in such a way that the problem is simplified, not made more complicated." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065446 #edb/ref 1065 896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065446 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e7845bcc-bef4-5a31-8abe-39845317fbaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065446 #edb/ref 1067 "Final Remark" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247437 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247437 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247437 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "022d7b7b-070a-51f5-bd49-94b4db34c49a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247834 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247834 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247834 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248350 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248350 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248350 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6729e761-a109-51c4-8606-18751a53f95b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248463 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{x}{2})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248463 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248463 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "76108c8b-8f42-5f4a-9dd2-e847f09e6e05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248678 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{3})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248678 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248678 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8bfdc77f-bbbe-57f4-9329-f07738aa11a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248682 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248682 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248682 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8cf1abf3-9f83-5499-84e8-2cdbf9e21301" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248985 #edb/ref 1080 "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248985 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248985 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aeaf0778-2cce-5ff4-8bd6-a8910cbdb116" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249108 #edb/ref 1080 "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249108 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249108 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249185 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-1)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249185 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249185 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c6440ae3-1132-5195-b3a2-356c7752e48e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249190 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249190 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249190 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c70e5714-4c05-5edb-b661-6e6122f8d589" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186249108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186249190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186249108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249964 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a7740ab9-c0ff-5f8c-91e3-87881adad76e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186247437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186247834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186248678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186249185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186247834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250086 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eede1f3b-85f2-5008-b473-3fcd59ae080b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250225 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186250086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250225 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250225 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250225 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250225 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "872e80da-db87-5cbe-89ef-83c58a2b3950" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250225 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{3}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & ={3}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{3}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186249964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250229 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250229 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250229 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8a77892-fbcb-5fb9-802a-ce425028c881" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250229 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257210 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257210 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257210 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257288 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257288 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257288 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "394ffebc-fc15-59d2-b922-cf67e8668a24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258130 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258130 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258130 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "98f26b34-1c20-50e4-ae9f-0696b345d0e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258723 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258723 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258723 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dee11791-9fa1-5f13-86b4-6751c7ac156e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258975 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258975 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258975 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa7bf65f-10a0-5fb7-85b0-318f615